.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt CAFFEINATE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm caffeinate
.Nd keep the machine from sleeping
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dimsu
.Op Fl t Ar timeout
.Op Fl w Ar pid
.Op Ar utility Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
holds power assertions that keep the machine, or its display, from going
to sleep: while
.Ar utility
runs (its exit status is
.Nm Ns 's),
until process
.Ar pid
exits, for
.Ar timeout
seconds, or else until it is interrupted.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Keep the display from sleeping when idle.
.It Fl i
Keep the system from sleeping when idle (the default).
.It Fl m
Keep the disks from sleeping when idle.
.It Fl s
Keep the system from sleeping at all, on AC power.
.It Fl u
Declare that the user is active (for 5 seconds unless
.Fl t
says otherwise), which wakes the display.
.It Fl t Ar timeout
Hold them this many seconds.
.It Fl w Ar pid
Hold them until process
.Ar pid
exits.
.El
.Pp
Where no power manager is running there is no sleep to prevent, and
.Nm
only waits.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pmset 1
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
